T*
(A short summary of the course: from your first program to pointers, classes and inheritance.) Tj T*
T*
(Week 1-2) Tj T*
(Setup and Hello World) Tj T*
(Install a compiler \(g++, clang or MSVC\). Every program starts at main. Include <iostream> and) Tj T*
(print with std::cout << "Hello" << std::endl;. Compile with g++ main.cpp -o app.) Tj T*
T*
(Variables and Data Types) Tj T*
(Common types are int, double, char, bool and std::string. Declare with int age = 25;. A) Tj T*
(variable keeps its type, and const makes a value unchangeable.) Tj T*
T*
(Control Flow) Tj T*
(Use if / else, switch, for, while and do-while. break leaves a loop and continue skips to) Tj T*
(the next round. Combine conditions with &&, || and !.) Tj T*
T*
(Functions) Tj T*
(A function has a return type, a name and parameters. Declare a prototype before use. Parameters) Tj T*
(are passed by value, or by reference with & to avoid copies. Functions can be overloaded.) Tj T*
T*
(Week 3-4) Tj T*
(Arrays and Strings) Tj T*
(Arrays have a fixed size \(int nums[5]\) and start at index 0. C++ does not check bounds.) Tj T*
(std::vector and std::string are safer and more flexible, and offer .size\(\).) Tj T*
T*
(Pointers) Tj T*
(A pointer stores a memory address. &x gives the address of x and *p reads the value at p. Use) Tj T*
(nullptr for empty pointers. Prefer smart pointers like std::unique_ptr over raw new and) Tj T*
(delete.) Tj T*
T*
(Classes and Objects) Tj T*
(A class bundles data and functions. Constructors initialize objects, and public / private control) Tj T*
(access. Inside a method, this points to the current object.) Tj T*
T*
(Inheritance) Tj T*
(A derived class reuses a base class: class Dog : public Animal. virtual functions enable) Tj T*
(polymorphism, and base classes used polymorphically need a virtual destructor.) Tj T*
T*
(Quick reference) Tj T*
(std::cout << x                        Print a value) Tj T*
(std::cin >> x                         Read a value) Tj T*
(&x                                    Address of x) Tj T*
(*p                                    Value pointed to by p) Tj T*
